<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>12</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.11.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Compile the uplink's own files directly rather than ProjectReference the
       net48 main csproj from a net10.0 test project, which would raise the
       cross-TFM NU1702 resolution warning. The whole uplink is KSP-free (no
       KSP/Unity reference at all; see the main csproj's header), so there is no
       split: every file in the main project compiles headlessly. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\mod\IAgxApi.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\mod\AgxReflection.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\mod\AgxActionGroupsBackend.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\mod\ActionGroupsExtendedUplink.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Sitrep.Contract, and nothing else of Gonogo's: the same one-line compile
    surface the Uplink itself has, which is what makes this suite travel with the
    Uplink instead of being left behind by it.

    It used to reference Sitrep.Host (for ChannelEngine/UplinkDiscovery and the
    ActionGroups election helper) and Sitrep.Contract.TestSupport (for
    StarvationProbeHost), dragging Sitrep.Core, Sitrep.Transport and
    Sitrep.Propagation along transitively without naming any of them, which
    docs/building.md recorded as this repo's widest open contradiction of the
    isolation rule. All three needs are gone rather than excused: the capability
    id moved to Sitrep.Contract (ActionGroupsCapability), the engine-ordering
    cases were asserting core's own two-pass discovery and moved to core's own
    suite, and the host double is RecordingUplinkHost.cs here.

    So this project wants no GonogoDevkit at all, which is the shape an outside
    author can reproduce: a vendored Sitrep.Contract.dll and nothing else.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Reference Include="Sitrep.Contract">
      <HintPath>$(GonogoContract)\netstandard2.0\Sitrep.Contract.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
